Permanode type:

camliNodeType: "importer"
importerType: "twitter"
authClientID:     "xxx"    // e.g. api token
authClientSecret: "sdkojfsldfjlsdkf"

camliNodeType: "importerAccount"
importerType: "twitter"
twitterAccount: "bradfitz"

Scratch caches
--------------

RunContext and SetupContext provide two automatically scoped sorted.KeyValue
caches, opened on demand:

- ImporterCache is shared by all accounts of one registered importer.
- AccountCache is private to one importer account, identified by its permanode.

Both methods return (sorted.KeyValue, error). Both scopes can use plain keys
such as "ratelimit" without colliding with other importers, accounts, or the
other scope. Reads, writes, batches, and scans stay in the selected scope.
Close on a cache view returns nil without closing its backing store.

These are disposable scratch caches, NOT authoritative importer state.
Even when persisted, they are not stored, indexed, or replicated in the main
blob storage. A cache may be missing, stale, deleted, or unavailable. An
importer must remain correct without it: cache contents may accelerate work,
but must not be the only record of progress, credentials, or imported data.
Reindexing or restoring blobs does not restore these caches. Strava uses
ImporterCache for its application-wide rate-limit snapshots.

With a configured local blobPath, the server defaults to:

    <blobPath>/importer-cache/strava/cache.sqlite
    <blobPath>/importer-cache/strava-sha224-<account-digest>/cache.sqlite

The importer-wide directory is the registered importer name; the account
directory appends its permanode blobref. Usual lowercase names stay readable;
unusual names are percent-escaped to avoid path and namespace collisions.
The backend follows the file-based index type (sqlite, leveldb, or kv),
defaulting to sorted.DefaultKVFileType when the index has no file-based
backend. LevelDB uses a cache.leveldb directory containing its own files
rather than one SQLite file. Stores and directories are created only when a
cache is first requested, not when the server starts.

Without a local blobPath, the default is memory-only; there is no fallback
to $HOME/.cache. The low-level importer handler can choose a local root and
backend explicitly:

    "handler": "importer",
    "handlerArgs": {
        "cacheRoot": "/srv/perkeep/blobs/importer-cache",
        "cacheType": "sqlite"
    }

cacheType supports sqlite, leveldb, and kv, and defaults to
sorted.DefaultKVFileType. An empty cacheRoot means memory-only. Separate
hosts should use separate roots. Stop the server before deleting stores.

For embedding and tests, HostConfig.CacheRoot and CacheType configure the
same on-demand file stores. HostConfig.Cache can instead inject a backing
sorted.KeyValue whose caller owns its lifetime; it cannot be combined with
CacheRoot or CacheType. Without either option, each importer and account
gets its own memory store, created on demand just like disk stores. Only an
explicitly injected backing store shares storage via prefixed views.

Host.Close cancels managed importer runs and long polls, waiting up to one
second for them to return and owned stores to close. On timeout it returns
an error; background cleanup leaves stores open until managed work returns,
then closes them. Repeated Close calls return the original result, even if
cleanup later finishes. Stop direct users of the Host, including independently
invoked Importer.Run calls, before closing it.
